    "body": "Owner update (2026-11-25): he does not know how the LN2W control cuts a corner under `G51` / `G52`. He will look at it on the machine's graphics display tomorrow.\n\nHe does not use `G51` himself: it lets the control decide the corner rounding and similar details, so the output is not fully known from the program. He says it is the easier way, though.\n\nThis supports the refusal in the current post. Item 2 (corner motion) stays open until the owner reports what the graphics show. A second route to keep in mind: a program that states the top and bottom path explicitly (4-axis X Y U V), so CamCraft decides each corner and the verify step checks the same surface the machine cuts. Ask the owner which route he uses for tapers before choosing.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
