    "body": "Owner input (2026-11-25), summarised in our own words:\n\n**The owner cuts tapers as 4-axis programs, not with `G51` / `G52`.** He uses `G74` (4-axis on) with an explicit U/V position on each move, and `G75` (4-axis off) at the end. He avoids `G51` because the control then decides the corner shape.\n\n**`TP` / `TN` in each mode:**\n\n| Mode | `TP` (table to program) | `TN` (table to next) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `G51`/`G52`, die face up, size held at the top | part thickness (less the die land, if any) | 0 |\n| `G51`/`G52`, die face down, size held at the bottom | 0 (or the die land) | part thickness |\n| `G74` 4-axis | height of the part bottom above the table (usually 0) | height of the part top above the table (usually the thickness). **Required in 4-axis**: it sets the U/V plane. |\n\n**Proposed route for this issue: 4-axis first.**\n- CamCraft computes the bottom path (X Y) and the top path, and writes U V = top minus bottom on each move, between `G74` and `G75`.\n- `TP` = part bottom above the table, and `TN` = part top above the table, from the setup (item 1).\n- CamCraft then decides every corner, and verify checks the same surface that the machine cuts. That removes item 2 (corner motion) for this route.\n- Lean side (item 3) becomes the sign of U/V, which a golden test can check against the top path.\n- `G51`/`G52` stays refused until the owner confirms the corner motion on the machine graphics.\n\nWaits for PR #4065 to merge (same post).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
