    "body": "fix on issue/4075-ln2w-4axis-taper · PR #4171 · pinned by script_sodick_ln2w::taper::* (7 tests), wire_post::sodick_aq600l::the_ln2w_taper_part_posts_as_a_four_axis_program_with_the_table_height, wire_post::sodick_aq600l::the_ln2w_taper_part_is_refused_by_name_without_the_table_height · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR is stacked on #4139. It uses the owner's 4-axis form: TP / TN, G74, U V on each move, G75. G51 / G52 stays refused. The table height is a post option (partBottomAboveTable) for now, not a per-setup value. The PR body and docs/decisions/4075-ln2w-4axis-taper.md give the reason.\n",
